  "summary": "The Menlo Park City Council on Sept. 26, 2023 declined to adopt Flock automated license plate readers, citing privacy concerns, cost (an initial $284,900 plus $251,000/year for 36 cameras), and questions about efficacy. The article contrasts Menlo Park's decision with neighboring Atherton, Woodside, and Redwood City, which recently approved Flock ALPR contracts.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The council decided not to consider installing ALPRs unless new data proves their efficacy in deterring crime.",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock ALPRs only use one-tenth of 1% of data collected, and the rest is deleted",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Redwood City's Council approved a $243,750 contract with Flock Safety on Sept. 11, to install 25 ALPR devices at key points in the city.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
